## Inheritance & `super()`

A subclass inherits from a base class and can call the parent's methods via `super()`:

```python
class Employee:
    def __init__(self, name, salary):
        self.name = name
        self.salary = salary

    def get_role(self):
        return "Standard Employee"

class Manager(Employee):
    def __init__(self, name, salary, bonus):
        super().__init__(name, salary)  # call parent __init__
        self.bonus = bonus

    def get_role(self):  # Method overriding
        return "Manager"

    def total_compensation(self):
        return self.salary + self.bonus
```

